    {
      "title": "TEST PROCEDURE",
      "items": [
        {
          "type": "textarea",
          "key": "test_procedure",
          "label": "Test Procedure",
          "default": "The test procedure was in accordance with <Standard name>.\n\nThe EUT was tested at the EFT test site with a ground GRP. The EFT generator was bonded directly to GND. The EUT was placed above 0.1m insulation which is in turn placed on the GRP.\n\nPower Line: The power supply to the EUT was fed through an inbuilt CDN of the EFT generator. EFT generator injects the transients through the CDN which was superimposed on to the power line of the EUT with reference to ground plane. During the test, performance of EUT was monitored as per the criteria specified in standard.\n\nSignal Line: The signal cable between the EUT and auxiliary equipment was routed through the capacitive coupling clamp, and the transients were coupled from the EFT generator through a HV cable connected to capacitive clamp. EFT generator injects the transients through the capacitive coupling clamp which was superimposed on to the signal cables of the EUT with reference to ground plane. During the test, performance of EUT was monitored as per the criteria specified in standard."
        }
      ]
    },
